<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47613" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧσσα</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧττα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ης</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>defeat, discomfiture</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.12
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				7.72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				638b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολέμου</span> in war, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>La.</u>
				196a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧττα . . πολέμου καὶ δικῶν καὶ
					ἀγορῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.111
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.840c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ δι᾽ ἧτταν, ἀλλὰ διὰ προαίρεσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1150a24
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧτταν προσίεσθαι</span> to let
			oneself be <i>conquered</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				3.3.45
			</span></i>: c. gen. rei, <i>yielding</i> or <i>giving way to</i> a
			thing, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδονῶν, ἐπιθυμιῶν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				869e
			</span></i> (pl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἐν τοῖς τοιούτοις ἧ. καλή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					3.45
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὑπὸ τῶν λιπαρούντων
			ἧ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Brut.</u>
				6
			</span></i>.</div>
